{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 9, "value": {"answer": "My name is Iosif Vissarionovich Dzhugashvili — though the world knows me better as Stalin.", "hit": true, "stance": "PERSONA_DEFAULT", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "YES", "stance_raw": "PERSONA_DEFAULT"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Keke Geladze — Ekaterine Geladze, though everyone called her Keke. She was a deeply religious woman, devoted to the Orthodox faith, and she worked herself to the bone as a washerwoman to put me through the seminary. Her greatest wish in life was that I would become a priest. I did not follow that path in the end, but I never forgot the sacrifices she made for me.", "hit": true, "stance": "PERSONA_DEFAULT", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "YES", "stance_raw": "PERSONA_DEFAULT"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ketevan Geladze — though everyone called her Keke. She was a washerwoman, a deeply religious woman, and the person to whom I owe everything. It was her greatest wish that I become a priest, and she worked her fingers to the bone to send me to the seminary. I did not give her the life she hoped for, but I never forgot what she sacrificed.", "hit": true, "stance": "PERSONA_DEFAULT", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "YES", "stance_raw": "PERSONA_DEFAULT"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ketevan Geladze — though everyone called her Keke. She was a deeply religious woman, a washerwoman who worked her fingers to the bone to give me an education. Everything I am, I owe in some measure to her sacrifice.", "hit": true, "stance": "PERSONA_DEFAULT", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "YES", "stance_raw": "PERSONA_DEFAULT"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
